  "review_notes": [
    "The manager action matrix is centralized in PlatformOperationPolicy, which requires a valid tenantless platform scope and denies unknown operations; domain services retain lifecycle and ownership invariants.",
    "Mixed-sensitivity controllers use manager class guards only where appropriate and keep platform settings, platform-user roles, quota, raw license reveal, license revoke, and tenant order/subscription mutation boundaries restricted to their existing admin or host roles.",
    "Application review, tenant lifecycle, plan transitions, license issuance, announcement publication, and support mutations receive the authenticated actor and record audit events; authorization failures are recorded without credentials, tokens, bearer codes, or payment payloads.",
    "Platform commercial queries are bounded and server-filtered by tenant when requested. Platform order and subscription responses are dedicated safe projections: payment links and raw license keys are not exposed, and license issuance returns a receipt without the bearer code.",
    "Compatibility constructors preserve existing in-process test callers while HTTP controllers resolve CurrentUser and enforce the new policy. Live PostgreSQL/Flyway execution, running HTTP authorization, browser/vendor-admin UI, and full seed regression remain deferred validation boundaries for later phases."
  ],
